Transcribro per-call preview suppression (2026-09-21).

Base: Moonshine 0.1.5 source revision
234f60faa0eb388b01cdf7e60aca232af37aefda, after Transcribro's existing
VAD-overlap, final-full-encode, and streaming-token-budget patches.

Local extension flag: MOONSHINE_FLAG_SKIP_INCOMPLETE_DECODING (1u << 2).
Pass it to moonshine_transcribe_stream only when current analysis should
skip tentative decoding under backlog. Public C signatures, struct layouts,
and the original four-argument internal entry point remain unchanged.
Default behavior is unchanged when this flag is absent.

Adapted upstream files (MIT; preserve the existing Moonshine license):
https://github.com/moonshine-ai/moonshine/blob/234f60faa0eb388b01cdf7e60aca232af37aefda/core/moonshine-c-api.h
https://github.com/moonshine-ai/moonshine/blob/234f60faa0eb388b01cdf7e60aca232af37aefda/core/transcriber.h
https://github.com/moonshine-ai/moonshine/blob/234f60faa0eb388b01cdf7e60aca232af37aefda/core/transcriber.cpp

Changes: optional per-call unfinished decoder suppression after frontend and
encoder advancement; retain the same line's text/word metadata under the
existing output lock; completed lines keep normal decoding and token bounds.
No shared option mutation, thread changes, new buffers, or text heuristics.
The adapted source paths and extended C header are recorded in CREDITS and
the independent Moonshine modification notice. JNI uses the generated,
patched C header from the same source tree as the runtime.

